## Expand → backfill → contract

```
1. expand  (compatible with old and new code)
2. deploy code using the new structure — API and {{workers}}
3. backfill
4. deploy code that stops using the old structure
5. contract (drop old) — a later migration
```

## Checklist for every migration

- [ ] Existing tables changed with `ALTER`; statements guarded so a rerun is safe
- [ ] Defaults / nullability for rows that already exist
- [ ] Unique / FK / check constraints checked against existing data first
- [ ] Lock impact on {{hot_tables}} estimated; online index builds where supported
- [ ] Backfills batched, resumable, scoped by {{scope_columns}}, values as bind parameters
- [ ] No secret values; personal data changes flagged for review
- [ ] A deployed migration is never edited — add a new one

